From f9f14498e8920d8503f03df7903e1e267a51c61a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 01:16:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] i686: implement GCC -mregparm=3 ABI end-to-end (callee
 capture, i64 pairs, reg structs, sret-in-eax, indirect calls); fix unsound
 ESP-offset never-read-store elimination
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The regparm callee side previously read register parameters from the
caller's stack frame — every -mregparm=3 program whose callee actually
used a register parameter was miscompiled. This blocked the Linux
kernel realmode/boot path (REALMODE_CFLAGS passes -mregparm=3).

Classification (call_abi.rs):
* new gcc_regparm_mode config replicating GCC function_arg_32:
  variadic => all args stack; I64/U64 => consecutive GP pair or
  stack+kill; overflow kills remaining regs; FP scalars skip GP regs
  without killing; aggregates take ceil(size/4) regs or stack+kill
  (verified against gcc -m32 -mregparm=3 on 20+ probe signatures).
* classify_args_core now receives real_variadic separately from the
  force_gp flag (the callee wrapper passes true unconditionally there).

i686 backend:
* prologue: two-phase register-param capture — phase 1 stores register
  params to memory homes (typed, sign/zero-extended) BEFORE any stack
  param copy can clobber %eax/%edx/%ecx; phase 2 resolves reg-to-reg
  captures as a parallel move with xchg cycle breaking.
* emit_param_ref: register params with eliminated allocas are
  pre-stored; the old fallback read caller-frame garbage — now a
  debug_assert + no-op.
* calls: I64RegPair and StructByValReg caller-side loading in
  descending base-register order (staging-safe); indirect calls under
  regparm call through the value's home instead of clobbering %eax.
* sret: hidden pointer travels in %eax under regparm>=1 (GCC
  semantics); callee emits plain ret, caller cleans up nothing.

Peephole:
* eliminate_never_read_stores compared raw N(%esp) offsets across ESP
  adjustments, deleting live capture stores (a store at 20(%esp)
  read back after two pushes as 28(%esp) looked dead). ESP offsets
  are now normalized to frame-anchored coordinates via a linear
  sp_down walk; calls and irregular ESP writes degrade conservatively.

Validation: 780/780 unit tests, 50/50 correctness suite, new
regparm3_abi_conformance.c green at -O0/-O1/-O2/-Os and under cdecl.
