MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every global scalar access on i686 paid address materialization plus an
indirect access (movl $sym,%edx; movl (%edx),%eax — 10 bytes, 2 regs)
where GCC emits movl sym,%eax (5 bytes, 0 extra regs). The shared
generation.rs fold infrastructure (global_addr_map, GEP offset merge,
foldable-use analysis) was already target-independent; i686 simply never
opted in.

* supports_global_addr_fold: true in non-PIC mode (PIC keeps the
  @GOT/@GOTOFF path through emit_global_addr).
* emit_global_load_abs: typed movl/movzbl/movswl sym, reg with
  register-direct destination; I64/F64 pairs via sym / sym+4.
* emit_global_store_abs: immediate stores fold to movb/movw/movl
  $imm, sym (no register at all); register-direct sources use the
  matching partial register when one exists (bl/cl/dl; si/di/bp for
  16-bit), %eax staging otherwise.

Realmode C corpus: 40737 -> 38738 bytes (GCC 12999; 3.13x -> 2.98x).
Validation: 780/780 unit, 50/50 correctness, regparm+cdecl ABI tests
green; x86-64 GOTPCREL paths unchanged.
